bpftune (0.4.67) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * revert the 0.4.64 port-based origin gate.

    0.4.64 filtered remote_port==443 || 80 to skip origin-facing
    sockets.  That assumed the VPS dials a CDN on 443.  On this
    topology the client-facing stream is VPS->home, and the port
    test was dropping the sockets the tuner is meant to tune.
    Symptom: swap rate flat at ~6/h across 5%->100% explore.

    Reverts to the 0.4.42 data_segs direction heuristic.  That leaked
    ~9% on the 0.4.63 window; the leak is real but small, and prior
    to 0.4.64 the tuner worked at this rate.  Any future direction
    test must be validated against this topology: remote_port is not
    a reliable discriminator when the VPS is the server on 443.

