bpftune (0.4.62) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * swap_score: initialize to SWAP_SCORE_NEUTRAL (256) the first time an
    algorithm runs on a bucket.  Previously an untested algorithm held
    swap_score == 0 in the map and pass-3 substituted 256 at decision
    time.  That substitution worked for the picker but not for the state
    file or any other reader -- the dashboard showed 0, which reads as
    "tested and bottomed out".  Both meanings are now distinct in the
    map: 256 = untested-or-neutral, 0 = decayed to zero (unreachable in
    practice for the fast-decay loss branch).
    No STATE_VERSION bump.  Existing state loads unchanged; existing
    zero-score algorithms get initialized on their next socket.

