bpftune (0.4.32) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Reference-drift fix: gate reference updates on sustained-transfer
    evidence, and allow the reference to recover upward via a streak
    of 5 consecutive far-better readings.
    - Down-drift observed: DNS, ctrl-API, SSH keepalives deliver
      tiny rates (88K-350K).  Their heal-down rule (rate < ref/3)
      pulled max_rate_delivered toward control-plane rates.
      Overnight on the home bucket this collapsed the ref from
      ~20M to 1.68M.
    - Up-lock observed: once collapsed, real traffic at 5-10M sits
      above ref*2 = 3.36M, so the outlier-rejection rule refused to
      accept it.  Nothing could move the ref up.
    - Fix part 1: new REF_TIME_CHECK_MIN_SEGS (2000) gates
      time-check reference updates.  Segment-rung votes (>= 10K
      segments) pass naturally.  Control-plane sockets cannot
      reach 2000.
    - Fix part 2: streak promotion.  Consecutive readings far past
      the ref (rate > ref*2, or rtt < ref/2) accumulate; at
      REF_HIGH_STREAK_N (5) in a row, promote the reference to the
      max (rate) or min (rtt) of the streak.  A single anomalous
      reading is still rejected.
    - Fix part 3: the same gate applies to the heal-down (rate)
      and heal-up (rtt) paths.  Control sockets cannot drag the
      reference in either direction.
  * struct remote_host gains rate_high_streak, rate_high_max,
    rtt_low_streak, rtt_low_min.
  * STATE_VERSION 9 -> 10.  State file MUST be deleted on
    deploy.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.31) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Per-socket freeze after FREEZE_AFTER_SWAPS (4) swaps.
    A socket that has cycled through four different algorithms
    without stabilising has a path or application problem that
    no algorithm choice can fix.  Once swap_count reaches the
    threshold, swap to whichever algorithm produced the lowest
    metric on THIS socket, set frozen=1, and skip moderate swaps
    for the rest of the connection.  Desperate readings (>= 2x the
    leader) still fire: the freeze insulates only against moderate
    churn, not against genuine path degradation.
  * conn_state gains best_seen_metric, best_seen_alg, frozen.
    best_seen_metric/alg update on every vote; the freeze path
    reads them.  Skips the ~0 poisoned-metric and 0 unset
    sentinels.
  * freeze log line emitted (tag=freeze) so the pattern is
    visible in the met log alongside swap lines.
  * STATE_VERSION 8 -> 9.  State file MUST be deleted on
    deploy.

