bpftune (0.4.24) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Vote at every checkpoint at or above METRIC_TRIGGER_SEGS, not just
    10K.  A socket that survives to 1M segments now casts five votes
    (10K/25K/100K/500K/1M) instead of one.  Long-lived sockets weigh
    more than short ones in proportion to their evidential value — the
    30-minute video and the 200 ms TLS handshake no longer contribute
    equally.  METRIC_AVG_CAP=32 bounds any single socket to ~15%% of an
    algorithm mean, so proportional weighting cannot drown the pack.

